Q: Mysql Like bind_param() on a non-object A: <p>Try this:</p>

<pre><code>$stmt=$mysqli-&gt;prepare('SELECT `title` FROM `post` WHERE (`content` LIKE ?) and accepted=0 order by count desc Limit 0,5');

$stmt-&gt;bind_param('s',$id);

$id = '%gsf%'; //The **%** go here

$stmt-&gt;execute();
$stmt-&gt;bind_result($title);

while( $stmt-&gt;fetch() ) {
      echo $title."&lt;br&gt;";         
}

$stmt-&gt;close();
$mysqli-&gt;close();
</code></pre>

Q: How to copy array without references in Type script? A: <p>You can use also <code>Object.assign</code>:</p>
<pre><code>this.records = Object.assign([], this.dataSource.data);
</code></pre>

Q: Exhaustive typechecking for `@switch` blocks in Angular? A: <p>In v21.2 Angular added support for exaustive typechecking in <code>@switch</code> blocks with the <code>@default never;</code> statement:</p>
<p>No need to define a method in the component now.</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>@switch (state.kind) {
  @case ('idle') {
    &lt;p&gt;Idle&lt;/p&gt;
  }

  @case ('loading') {
    &lt;p&gt;Loading…&lt;/p&gt;
  }

  @case ('success') {
    &lt;!-- state is narrowed --&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Result: {{ state.data }}&lt;/p&gt;
  }

  @case ('error') {
    &lt;!-- state is narrowed --&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Error: {{ state.message }}&lt;/p&gt;
  }

  @default never; &lt;!-- Enables exhaustive typecheking here --&gt; 
}
</code></pre>
